<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 63,780 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 63,780 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 63,780 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 53,764 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 6,526	   18,304</p>
<p>    Import cargo			57,254	   35,460</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, one ship sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships were expected to sail and four were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Feul oil		 50,000	 Al Safa	     25/1</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,090	 Johar		 26/1</p>
<p>Sugar		     7,500	 Faurei		 due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 15,000	 Wawasan Megah     29/1</p>
<p>High speed deisel    27,300	 Chilham Castle    24/1</p>
<p>Chemicals		10,550	 Bakri Orbitor     29/1</p>
<p>Gas oil		  56,000	 Keefan		26/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
